{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And I said</b> — like 'I said in my heart.' The word יְשׁוּפֵנִי is from the root נשף. And if they are two roots, like 'for they are circumcised and you are circumcised,' and others like it." "<b>Behold יְשׁוּפֵנִי</b> — like 'it will hide me.' The meaning: perhaps the darkness will hide me so that You will not see what I do, or think." "<b>And the word יְשׁוּפֵנִי</b> — draws another [interpretation], like 'and the prophecy of Oded the prophet.' <b>And behold, night will become light around me</b> — and this is light in its plain sense. And R. Moses said: all the night will be light around me. And the correct in my eyes: that which I mentioned and the proof —"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 139, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:11.684986126Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}